cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SPACEMAP Studio: a spatial multiplex imaging analysis pipeline"
message: >-
  If you use SPACEMAP in your research, please cite the paper listed under
  preferred-citation.
type: software

# Authors of the SOFTWARE. This is the development credit, and is separate
# from the paper's author list below. Bassel Dawod wrote the code; Todd A.
# Aguilera is the senior author and principal investigator.
authors:
  - given-names: Bassel
    family-names: Dawod
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Radiation Oncology, University of Texas Southwestern
      Medical Center
    email: basbees@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1055-4387"
  - given-names: Todd
    name-particle: A.
    family-names: Aguilera
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Radiation Oncology, University of Texas Southwestern
      Medical Center
    email: todd.aguilera@utsouthwestern.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3734-3758"

repository-code: "https://github.com/AguileraLab/SPACEMAP"
url: "https://github.com/AguileraLab/SPACEMAP"
abstract: >-
  SPACEMAP is an end-to-end pipeline for spatial multiplex imaging analysis,
  covering image registration, background subtraction, ROI extraction, tissue
  annotation, cell segmentation, batch correction, immune phenotyping and
  spatial analysis, through a graphical interface and reusable Python modules.
  It includes an optional, local-first AI assistant that is disabled by
  default.
keywords:
  - spatial biology
  - multiplex imaging
  - CODEX
  - cell segmentation
  - phenotyping
  - bioimage analysis
license-url: "https://github.com/AguileraLab/SPACEMAP/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: 0.4.0
# Add date-released when the Studio release is published.

# The publication describing the method. GitHub's "Cite this repository"
# button and most reference managers prefer this over the software entry.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Resolving phenotyping discordance with SPACEMAP, an integrated machine
    learning framework
  authors:
    - given-names: Bassel
      family-names: Dawod
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1055-4387"
    - given-names: Arely
      family-names: Perez Rodriguez
    - given-names: Sebastian
      family-names: Diegeler
    - given-names: Eslam
      family-names: Elghonaimy
    - given-names: Megan
      family-names: Wachsman
    - given-names: Purva
      family-names: Gopal
    - given-names: David
      family-names: Hein
    - given-names: Paul
      name-particle: H.
      family-names: Acosta
    - given-names: Andrew
      family-names: Jamieson
    - given-names: Gaudenz
      family-names: Danuser
    - given-names: Robert
      name-particle: D.
      family-names: Timmerman
    - given-names: Satwik
      family-names: Rajaram
    - given-names: Todd
      name-particle: A.
      family-names: Aguilera
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3734-3758"
  journal: bioRxiv
  year: 2025
  month: 12
  doi: "10.1101/2025.11.27.690631"
  url: "https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2025.11.27.690631v1"
  notes: >-
    Preprint. Update this entry with the journal reference once the paper is
    published.

